1.	Assume the first element is already sorted.
2.	Start an outer loop from index 1 to n-1.
3.	Treat array[i] as the current element.
4.	Set j = i.
5.	While j > 0 and array[j-1] > array[j]:
6.	Swap array[j] and array[j-1].
7.	Decrease j by 1.
8.	Continue until the correct position is found.
9.	After each pass, the subarray from 0 to i becomes sorted.
10.	Key Idea: Insert each element into its correct position in the sorted portion.

Time Complexity
Worst Case: O(n²)

Space Complexity
O(1)
